# Outputs (every run is reproducible from its inputs — don't commit)
#
# These used to carry `!output/supplier_params.csv` negations, intending to version
# the derived planning parameters. They never worked: git cannot re-include a file
# once a parent directory is excluded, so the two files were never tracked. The need
# they were reaching for — seeing when a SKU's lead time or stocking class moved — is
# served properly by the monthly snapshots in output/history/, which `feedback.drift`
# reads back.
output/
eval-workspace/

